  "description": "Forty-two short reports chosen by al-Nawawi to summarise the foundations of the religion, beginning with 'Actions are judged by intentions' and closing with the verse on the heart's turning. The collection became a standard first text in madrasa teaching and one of the most widely memorised hadith works.",
  "historicalContext": "Compiled in Damascus in the thirteenth century, when al-Nawawi was teaching hadith and law. Its forty reports were chosen for concision and legal weight rather than for exhaustiveness; later scholars wrote hundreds of commentaries on it, and its numbering is still used across schools.",
